    "dispositions": [
      "All new runtime scopes have complete scans with no high findings. LICENSE URLs are legal text. Code viewer RegExp.exec reads supported startLine metadata, not code execution.",
      "The UI browser driver starts only existing Chromium in a fresh tmpfs profile; its HTTP/CDP connections are namespace-local loopback. Environment reads are explicit isolation flags. The only writable output mount is docs/ui-previews. It mounts real plugin modules and CSS with controlled widget stand-ins; it does not mount or call the original app, account/model services or source checkout root.",
      "The original pure themes.ts is byte-identical to the pinned upstream file. Its only import is type-only; runtime is data, color/string helpers and theme variable construction. No package dependency, filesystem, network, process or environment access occurs. It supplies two built-in preset palettes only, never user settings.",
      "Network flags in home.tsx and sidebar.tsx refer to existing app API reads. Those files are only inert parser input in this experiment; their React imports, hooks and network operations are not executed.",
      "Existing native helper/TypeBox/Babel review evidence stays in native-lesson-intake.json and native-confidence-code-review.json. Exact bytes and advisories must be rechecked before helper reuse. No scanner limit or detector has changed."
    ],
